Why this change is acceptable when prior optimization attempts in this area were rejected (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35041#issuecomment-4217337173):
* First commit is a *higher level* change to combine two calls to `DecodeBase58Check()` into one.
* Second commit *trivially* replaces linear lookup with `O(1)` lookup table.

In my subjective view they have a lower impact on code readability than the rejected PRs. Also, the author of this PR motivates it through the concrete second-order effect of speeding up fuzz targets.

(I'm still open to reviewing further optimizations in this area, without guarantees of priority).

